 ## Verification
 
-`npm test` checks atomic writes, external-edit conflicts, missing-file behavior, session backup recovery, window position recovery, recent-file ordering, and compatibility with existing profiles. `node tests/desktop-smoke.cjs` exercises the actual Electron editor, native clipboard, compact menu layout, menu clipboard actions, file saves, recent files, page widths, font selection, actual plus/minus keyboard input in both views, source wrapping and wrapped Find, formatting-icon size isolation/persistence, multi-document View switching, separate undo/cursor/scroll state, fixed Find/Replace positioning, Save/Discard/Cancel on document close and exit, and recovery of every open document. The latter needs a graphical session or Xvfb on Linux.
+`npm test` checks atomic writes, external-edit conflicts, missing-file behavior, session backup recovery, window position recovery, recent-file ordering, compatibility with existing profiles, the right-click menu template, the smart typography rules (quotes, dashes, ellipses, and the Markdown regions they must leave alone), and Markdown escaping (including thousands of random strings of punctuation that marked must read back unchanged). `npm run test:equivalence` checks the performance paths against TipTap's stock code (see Performance). `npm run test:typography` exercises smart typography, the Heading 4 style, and the settings layout in the real Electron editor (graphical session or Xvfb). `node tests/desktop-smoke.cjs` exercises the actual Electron editor, native clipboard, compact menu layout, menu clipboard actions, file saves, recent files, page widths, font selection, actual plus/minus keyboard input in both views, source wrapping and wrapped Find, formatting-icon size isolation/persistence, multi-document View switching, separate undo/cursor/scroll state, fixed Find/Replace positioning, Save/Discard/Cancel on document close and exit, and recovery of every open document. The latter needs a graphical session or Xvfb on Linux.
 
-New installations keep recovery data under Electron's per-user app-data directory for Quill, separately from the original Scratch app. Quill detects and reuses a valid profile from the previous custom editor, preserving its draft, font, zoom, and other preferences. Previously saved preset page widths become Full; an existing Custom width is preserved. No account, AI model, cloud sync, updater, or analytics is configured. Remote images can be loaded if they appear in a document.
+New installations keep recovery data under Electron's per-user app-data directory for PicoMarQ, separately from the original Scratch app. PicoMarQ detects and reuses a valid profile from Quill (0.1.6–0.1.11) or the earlier custom editor, preserving open documents, drafts, recent files, font, zoom, and other preferences. Previously saved preset page widths become Full; an existing Custom width is preserved. No account, AI model, cloud sync, updater, or analytics is configured. Remote images can be loaded if they appear in a document.
 
