index 0ec7520..99e9f7a 100644
--- a/assets/ICON.md
+++ b/assets/ICON.md
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
-# Quill icon
+# PicoMarQ icon
 
-Approved concept C: an ivory serif Q with a sweeping tail on a rich plum rounded square. The transparent master PNG was made with the built-in image-generation tool from the approved concept board. `npm run build:icon` downsizes the master and creates the Windows ICO at 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 128, and 256 pixels.
+A white sheet with a folded top-right corner and a bold outline in PicoMarQ red (#870121), carrying the Markdown "M" (the letter from the public-domain Markdown mark) whose right stem runs on below the baseline into an arrowhead — the design was settled on 2026-10-10 after a round of comparisons at taskbar sizes.
 
-Generation prompt:
+- The sheet is almost square (98.5% of the icon's width) so the icon matches its neighbours for size; the dog-ear is what says "document", not the paper's proportions. The corners outside the sheet are transparent.
+- The glyph sits in the band between the bottom of the fold and the bottom of the sheet, as large as a 5% margin allows, and is centred on the M itself: the arrowhead's point past the right stem is ignored, so the letter looks centred.
+- `scripts/build-icon.cjs` holds the drawing and renders every size with Playwright's Chromium (`npm run build:icon`; `npx playwright install chromium` first, or set `PICOMARQ_CHROMIUM` to a Chromium binary). It writes `app.ico` with 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 128 and 256 px images (PNG-encoded; the two smallest use a heavier outline), `assets/app-icon.svg`, and the PNG copies `assets/app-icon.png` and `app-icon.png`. `npm run package:windows` embeds every size in the executable and verifies the embedded pixels against `app.ico`.
 
-> Use the attached icon concept board as the exact design reference. Produce ONLY option C, the Q monogram from the TOP RIGHT tile, as ONE standalone production-ready Windows application icon for Quill. Preserve its specific elegant ivory serif capital Q with the sweeping, tapered calligraphic tail in the lower right, its ivory coloring, its deep rich plum rounded-square background, its overall proportions, and its subtle restrained color shading. Reproduce option C faithfully, keeping the Q shape and thick/thin stroke character. The plum tile is the icon itself; keep that tile fully opaque with clean rounded corners. Fill almost the full square output canvas with the tile, maintaining square proportions and a narrow transparent margin on all sides. The four corners outside the rounded tile and the narrow outer margin MUST be truly transparent. Crop out every other concept, every caption, the board heading, and the white comparison-board background. No label, no additional text, no border, no shadow outside the tile, no new decoration, no desktop mockup. Center the final icon precisely in a square canvas, rendering sharp smooth edges at high resolution so it can be downscaled to a multi-size Windows ICO. This is a precise-object edit extracting and finishing the approved C icon, not a redesign.
+Earlier icons: a plum-and-ivory Q monogram (Quill, builds 0.1.6–0.1.11) and a black-outline document with the M↓ mark on an opaque white square (0.1.12).
